Mr. Kunnu, this guy is a crazy guy.

1042
01:00:02,111 --> 01:00:03,697
He's a psychopath.

1043
01:00:03,777 --> 01:00:05,258
Take him out of the club,

1044
01:00:05,338 --> 01:00:07,207
or take him out of the UK.

1045
01:00:07,287 --> 01:00:08,428
Sorry, Tiny. Sorry.

1046
01:00:08,508 --> 01:00:10,394
What, "sorry Tiny?"

1047
01:00:10,768 --> 01:00:12,920
- His name is Tiny?
- Just sit down.

1048
01:00:13,997 --> 01:00:15,133
Drink this.

1049
01:00:15,213 --> 01:00:16,356
What's wrong with you?

1050
01:00:19,882 --> 01:00:20,846
Sorry.

1051
01:00:21,767 --> 01:00:22,986
Don't get stressed.

1052
01:00:24,609 --> 01:00:25,405
Preet.

1053
01:00:25,851 --> 01:00:27,039
Hi, Jass.

1054
01:00:27,483 --> 01:00:28,335
Hi.

1055
01:00:28,833 --> 01:00:29,955
Who is she?

1056
01:00:30,035 --> 01:00:30,903
She...

1057
01:00:33,165 --> 01:00:34,245
Preet, I'm Baani.

1058
01:00:35,091 --> 01:00:36,933
I was in Jass's life before you.

1059
01:00:37,119 --> 01:00:38,661
And we were married to each other.

1060
01:00:39,063 --> 01:00:41,397
He wanted a baby, and I didn't.

1061
01:00:41,559 --> 01:00:43,538
So we separated, but...

1062
01:00:43,951 --> 01:00:45,445
now I'm carrying his baby.

1063
01:00:46,095 --> 01:00:47,433
Jass told me about--

1064
01:00:56,457 --> 01:00:58,515
My brother only holds a gun,

1065
01:00:59,751 --> 01:01:00,849
but I fire.

1066
01:01:04,197 --> 01:01:05,619
What are you doing, Preet?
Have you lost your mind?

1067
01:01:05,877 --> 01:01:08,091
Preet, you're making
a big mistake by killing him.

1068
01:01:08,893 --> 01:01:10,227
You're right.

1069
01:01:10,420 --> 01:01:12,021
I should kill you.

1070
01:01:13,280 --> 01:01:16,887
Baani!

1071
01:01:24,810 --> 01:01:26,592
Baby, are you okay?

1072
01:01:28,032 --> 01:01:28,878
What happened?

1073
01:01:28,958 --> 01:01:30,684
Why did you suddenly fall down?

1074
01:01:31,194 --> 01:01:32,387
No, I...

1075
01:01:32,773 --> 01:01:36,558
Dizziness and loss of balance
is common during pregnancy.

1076
01:01:36,638 --> 01:01:38,370
I'm the one who is pregnant.
Not you.

1077
01:01:38,450 --> 01:01:40,116
- Yeah.
- You're so funny.

1078
01:01:42,204 --> 01:01:43,055
Hey...

1079
01:01:43,656 --> 01:01:44,784
My brother!

1080
01:01:47,076 --> 01:01:50,940
I gave you permission
to go out with Preet.

1081
01:01:51,020 --> 01:01:52,956
But before marriage,
you've made my sister--

1082
01:01:53,199 --> 01:01:55,686
Sorry, Randhawa ji.
I should've asked permission.

1083
01:01:55,836 --> 01:01:57,984
It was a mistake made out of love.

1084
01:01:59,028 --> 01:02:01,530
Don't even think about doing it again.

1085
01:02:02,958 --> 01:02:05,856
Babies... should be born out of love.

1086
01:02:06,984 --> 01:02:08,238
So understanding.

1087
01:02:08,958 --> 01:02:10,480
Sire, the priest is here.

1088
01:02:11,466 --> 01:02:12,930
- Please come.
- The priest.

1089
01:02:13,386 --> 01:02:14,838
But why is the priest here?

1090
01:02:16,224 --> 01:02:19,087
Sir, have you found an auspicious day?

1091
01:02:20,161 --> 01:02:24,031
Oh, an auspicious date for the
baby's 'Naamkaran' (naming ceremony).

1092
01:02:24,218 --> 01:02:26,537
In fact, I think we
should name the boy Karan.

1093
01:02:26,617 --> 01:02:28,046
'Naam Karan'. Get it?

1094
01:02:28,126 --> 01:02:28,832
Good one.

1095
01:02:28,912 --> 01:02:31,112
The priest is here to
pick a date for the wedding.

1096
01:02:31,192 --> 01:02:32,830
Wedding? Whose?

1097
01:02:32,910 --> 01:02:34,240
Ours. Who else?

1098
01:02:34,600 --> 01:02:36,258
- Okay.
- Tell us, sir.

1099
01:02:36,461 --> 01:02:39,423
The first eight days
of next month are auspicious.

1100
01:02:39,503 --> 01:02:40,937
- Great.
- But I am not free.

1101
01:02:41,017 --> 01:02:43,068
- Are you busy?
- I am conducting several weddings.

1102
01:02:43,148 --> 01:02:44,314
- Brother.
- Guggi.

1103
01:02:44,394 --> 01:02:47,018
- Sire...
- Cancel all his weddings.

1104
01:02:47,279 --> 01:02:48,151
Sire.

1105
01:02:48,370 --> 01:02:50,598
There you go, sir.
Your schedule is clear.

1106
01:02:50,995 --> 01:02:53,387
Second marriage before
divorcing your first wife?

1107
01:02:55,300 --> 01:02:59,140
I'm the judge,
and I'll sentence him.

1108
01:02:59,351 --> 01:03:00,998
Death sentence!

1109
01:03:02,107 --> 01:03:03,228
This wedding is not possible.

1110
01:03:03,308 --> 01:03:05,006
This wedding is not possible at all.

1111
01:03:05,171 --> 01:03:08,216
Why? Are you busy as well,
just like the priest?

1112
01:03:08,793 --> 01:03:11,621
- Let me explain.
- Explain.

1113
01:03:12,477 --> 01:03:15,987
Randhawa ji, you must've
attended your father's wedding.

1114
01:03:16,067 --> 01:03:18,087
- You fool.
- Brother.

1115
01:03:18,167 --> 01:03:20,607
How can anyone attend
their father's wedding?

1116
01:03:20,687 --> 01:03:23,059
Exactly, sir.
That's what I am saying.

1117
01:03:23,225 --> 01:03:27,052
Fate is giving my child the
chance to attend my wedding, sir.

1118
01:03:27,132 --> 01:03:30,058
Just visualise, sir.
Happy family in one frame, sir.

1119
01:03:30,268 --> 01:03:33,336
Nephew Randhawa in uncle Randhawa's lap.

1120
01:03:33,531 --> 01:03:37,304
And our child, happy in a nappy,
will sing and dance.

1121
01:03:37,384 --> 01:03:40,078
Uncle and nephew spinning
around in the city of London.

1122
01:03:40,158 --> 01:03:42,492
Spinning... Spinning...

1123
01:03:42,572 --> 01:03:43,460
Enough!

1124
01:03:51,843 --> 01:03:52,755
Excellent!

1125
01:03:53,439 --> 01:03:56,467
Even the filmmaker Sooraj Barjatya
never had a vision like this.

1126
01:03:57,035 --> 01:03:58,325
It's an original idea.

1127
01:03:58,550 --> 01:03:59,825
What do you say, Preet?

1128
01:04:00,876 --> 01:04:02,036
Yes, I like it.

1129
01:04:02,240 --> 01:04:03,740
- You're happy, I'm happy.
- I like it. I'm happy.

1130
01:04:03,820 --> 01:04:05,735
It is decided.

1131
01:04:06,038 --> 01:04:09,458
First, the baby comes in a carriage,
then we'll dance at the marriage.

1132
01:04:09,649 --> 01:04:12,647
Right... uncle and nephew spinning
around in the city of London.

1133
01:04:12,727 --> 01:04:14,911
- Spinning.
- Spinning... Spinning...

1134
01:04:16,280 --> 01:04:17,704
- Bye.
- Bye, baby.

1135
01:04:31,114 --> 01:04:33,156
- Just call Jass.
- Baani.

1136
01:04:33,493 --> 01:04:34,416
Baani.

1137
01:04:34,836 --> 01:04:36,089
- What happened?
- She's in terrible pain.

1138
01:04:36,169 --> 01:04:39,002
- Hurry, take her to the hospital.
- Thank you, Martha, thank you.

1139
01:04:39,082 --> 01:04:41,324
- Take her to the hospital quickly.
- Careful.

1140
01:04:41,404 --> 01:04:42,190
Come, come.

1141
01:04:48,069 --> 01:04:50,105
- Are you okay, Baani?
- Yeah, I'm okay.

1142
01:04:50,185 --> 01:04:52,062
The hospital is nearby.

1143
01:04:56,413 --> 01:04:59,181
Baani, I want to tell you something.

1144
01:04:59,261 --> 01:05:00,177
Yeah.

1145
01:05:00,643 --> 01:05:02,293
I mean, I can tell you this later,

1146
01:05:03,222 --> 01:05:05,135
but I can't keep this inside me anymore.

1147
01:05:06,080 --> 01:05:10,092
When we separated...
you told me to move on.

1148
01:05:12,543 --> 01:05:15,453
Months later, I met a girl.

1149
01:05:16,503 --> 01:05:17,373
Preet.

1150
01:05:20,181 --> 01:05:21,489
We fell in love, Baani.

1151
01:05:23,547 --> 01:05:24,303
Baani...

1152
01:05:25,119 --> 01:05:26,307
Baani, are you listening...

1153
01:05:38,777 --> 01:05:39,774
What the hell!

1154
01:05:40,067 --> 01:05:41,154
But that's--

1155
01:05:41,234 --> 01:05:44,769
Sire, it's Jass...
your brother-in-law.

1156
01:05:45,085 --> 01:05:45,590
Brother-in-law?

1157
01:05:45,670 --> 01:05:46,622
- What?
- Jass?

1158
01:05:47,596 --> 01:05:49,194
Where is Jass going?

1159
01:05:50,348 --> 01:05:51,668
Who's honking here?

1160
01:05:54,650 --> 01:05:57,278
Randhawa? Where did he appear from?

1161
01:05:57,804 --> 01:06:00,798
Always bloody after me.

1162
01:06:04,998 --> 01:06:07,428
Sire, why is he driving so fast?

1163
01:06:07,754 --> 01:06:09,366
- Call him. Call him.
- Yes.

1164
01:06:10,754 --> 01:06:16,551
"Toasted. Toasted. Toasted."

1165
01:06:17,226 --> 01:06:18,474
He didn't answer, sire.

1166
01:06:19,128 --> 01:06:20,232
Call him again.

1167
01:06:20,728 --> 01:06:22,560
- 'The number you've called is switched off'
- It's okay.

1168
01:06:22,640 --> 01:06:24,234
Sire, it's switched off!

1169
01:06:24,522 --> 01:06:27,594
Sir, I'm a vegetarian,
but still I smell something fishy.

1170
01:06:27,674 --> 01:06:28,974
Just shut up, Guggi.

1171
01:06:29,214 --> 01:06:32,313
Brother. Speed up.
I'm feeling very, very uneasy.

1172
01:06:32,468 --> 01:06:34,218
Just take a deep breath, okay.

1173
01:06:38,949 --> 01:06:40,832
Who gives such people
a driving license?

1174
01:06:54,990 --> 01:06:56,985
Why did you stop, sire? Let's go.

1175
01:06:57,217 --> 01:06:59,573
This is London, not Ludhiana.

1176
01:07:01,406 --> 01:07:01,909
Damn!

1177
01:07:02,122 --> 01:07:03,375
We made it. We made it.

1178
01:07:03,455 --> 01:07:05,558
We overtook everyone
and made it to the hospital first.

1179
01:07:05,638 --> 01:07:07,770
Baani, wake up.
Come on, come on, fast.

1180
01:07:08,935 --> 01:07:09,715
Let's go, Baani.

1181
01:07:09,795 --> 01:07:10,808
Jass, I can't walk.

1182
01:07:10,888 --> 01:07:12,196
Don't worry.
We've reached the hospital.

1183
01:07:12,276 --> 01:07:13,313
- Let's go inside.
- Hold on.

1184
01:07:13,666 --> 01:07:17,188
Don't get stressed.
Selfie Kumar is here.

1185
01:07:17,268 --> 01:07:18,754
Sit. Sit down.

1186
01:07:18,834 --> 01:07:20,270
- Sir, where is the doctor?
- Wait a minute.

1187
01:07:20,350 --> 01:07:21,432
Are you the husband?

1188
01:07:21,658 --> 01:07:22,783
- Yes.
- Is she the wife?

1189
01:07:22,863 --> 01:07:24,832
- She's pregnant.
- That's life.

1190
01:07:24,912 --> 01:07:27,067
- Wait a minute.
- What are you doing?

1191
01:07:27,147 --> 01:07:28,769
Virtual registration.

1192
01:07:29,102 --> 01:07:30,861
Everything's digital now.

1193
01:07:30,941 --> 01:07:32,271
Now it's safely stored on my phone

1194
01:07:32,351 --> 01:07:34,868
that you're the husband
and she's your wife.

1195
01:07:35,139 --> 01:07:36,339
- Sir, we want to see the doctor...
- Hold on.

1196
01:07:36,419 --> 01:07:39,166
Sophie. Take the patient to Dr. Gulati.

1197
01:07:39,489 --> 01:07:40,427
- Please.
- Come.

1198
01:07:41,244 --> 01:07:43,539
Excuse me. Mr. Ahuja.

1199
01:07:43,619 --> 01:07:44,409
That's me, sir.

1200
01:07:44,489 --> 01:07:46,403
- Myself Dr. Gulati.
- Hi.

1201
01:07:46,726 --> 01:07:47,611
How is Baani?

1202
01:07:47,691 --> 01:07:50,323
Not Baani. A story, honey...

1203
01:07:50,559 --> 01:07:52,216
The story of a mother.

1204
01:07:52,374 --> 01:07:54,616
A mother carries her child
for nine months in her womb,

1205
01:07:55,123 --> 01:07:58,351
three years in her arms,
and a lifetime in her heart.

1206
01:07:58,546 --> 01:08:00,624
That's right, sir.
But please tell me how is Baani.

1207
01:08:00,704 --> 01:08:03,287
She's not Baani. She's love, honey...

1208
01:08:03,489 --> 01:08:05,162
A mother's love.

1209
01:08:06,032 --> 01:08:08,365
When a child kicks in the womb,

1210
01:08:08,544 --> 01:08:12,264
a mother's heart jumps with joy.

1211
01:08:12,344 --> 01:08:14,844
Sir, please tell me, how is Baani?

1212
01:08:14,924 --> 01:08:17,800
Why are you talking
about all this nonsense?

1213
01:08:17,980 --> 01:08:19,179
How is Baani?

1214
01:08:19,259 --> 01:08:20,557
Mr. Ahuja, relax.

1215
01:08:21,085 --> 01:08:23,965
Religiously speaking,
you should read these three books.

1216
01:08:24,130 --> 01:08:26,860
'Maa ki Mamta' written by Mamta's mother.
('A Mother's Love' written by a Mother)

1217
01:08:27,400 --> 01:08:28,406
My favourite...

1218
01:08:28,486 --> 01:08:30,348
'Nau Mahina With My Hasina'
(Nine Months With My Beloved)

1219
01:08:30,967 --> 01:08:35,054
And... 'Lalla Lalla Lori, Do Patang Ek Dori'
(The Lullaby Of Two Kites And Their String)

1220
01:08:35,134 --> 01:08:36,491
I've written this myself.

1221
01:08:39,197 --> 01:08:40,983
Listen, doctor.
I'm not here for an exam.

1222
01:08:41,063 --> 01:08:42,128
I've lost my patience.

1223
01:08:42,420 --> 01:08:43,898
- Did I ask you before becoming a father?
- No.

1224
01:08:43,978 --> 01:08:45,092
I am going to meet Baani.

1225
01:08:45,172 --> 01:08:47,108
I'm not asking you,
I'm telling you this.

1226
01:08:47,188 --> 01:08:48,121
Excuse me...

1227
01:08:48,695 --> 01:08:50,266
- Mr. Ahuja...
- What now?

1228
01:08:51,367 --> 01:08:52,366
Idiot.

1229
01:08:53,558 --> 01:08:56,655
He's definitely not ready
to become a father.

1230
01:09:03,217 --> 01:09:04,933
Your baby is fine.

1231
01:09:09,175 --> 01:09:11,441
Earlier, I didn't want a child, Jass.

1232
01:09:13,000 --> 01:09:16,112
But now, when this child
is coming into this world,

1233
01:09:17,553 --> 01:09:19,465
this child is my entire world.

1234
01:09:37,214 --> 01:09:39,045
Go to the cafeteria, Baani.
I'll join you in a bit.

1235
01:09:39,125 --> 01:09:39,959
Jass?

1236
01:09:56,605 --> 01:09:57,632
Brother.

1237
01:09:58,453 --> 01:10:00,039
I need to use the restroom.

1238
01:10:00,369 --> 01:10:01,412
Okay, go.

1239
01:10:02,763 --> 01:10:04,270
Alice, just come with me.

1240
01:10:04,350 --> 01:10:05,252
Let's go.

1241
01:10:06,888 --> 01:10:08,988
Oh... Oh, my God. Sorry.

1242
01:10:11,185 --> 01:10:12,573
What are you doing here?

1243
01:10:16,076 --> 01:10:16,931
Shitting.

1244
01:10:20,778 --> 01:10:22,405
Can you close the door?

1245
01:10:23,357 --> 01:10:26,815
Brother-in-law,
we've been waiting for a long time.

1246
01:10:27,954 --> 01:10:29,571
Come on, tell us.

1247
01:10:30,010 --> 01:10:30,873
Tell you what?

1248
01:10:31,030 --> 01:10:33,404
You were racing down the road,

1249
01:10:33,930 --> 01:10:35,567
you didn't hear us honking,

1250
01:10:35,647 --> 01:10:37,217
didn't answer the phone,

1251
01:10:37,865 --> 01:10:39,917
and even switched it off.

1252
01:10:40,351 --> 01:10:42,092
What's going on, brother-in-law?

1253
01:10:42,331 --> 01:10:47,659
Brother... truth is...
I love someone else more than Preet.

1254
01:10:48,353 --> 01:10:49,433
- What?
- Yes.

1255
01:10:49,598 --> 01:10:50,655
It's true.

1256
01:10:51,440 --> 01:10:54,054
Preet's happiness.
Her happiness.

1257
01:10:54,497 --> 01:10:57,662
She should get the right doctor,
right hospital, top-class treatment.

1258
01:10:57,820 --> 01:10:59,912
That's why I got here before you did.

1259
01:11:00,280 --> 01:11:01,382
- Jass.
- Yeah.

1260
01:11:02,836 --> 01:11:04,674
Do you see everything I'm doing for you?

1261
01:11:05,430 --> 01:11:08,082
- See, brother. He loves me so much.
- Yes.

1262
01:11:08,561 --> 01:11:10,652
- Mrs. Preet Randhawa?
- Yes.

1263
01:11:10,732 --> 01:11:12,796
Dr. Gulati is ready for you.

1264
01:11:12,876 --> 01:11:14,649
- He's calling you in.
- Let's go.

1265
01:11:14,729 --> 01:11:16,112
You guys sit here.

1266
01:11:16,192 --> 01:11:17,694
- You stay here.
- Okay.

1267
01:11:18,048 --> 01:11:19,488
Move him aside and come.

1268
01:11:19,660 --> 01:11:21,286
One second. Jass.

1269
01:11:21,528 --> 01:11:22,630
- Please come.
- Be careful.

1270
01:11:23,816 --> 01:11:25,180
This way, please.

1271
01:11:25,260 --> 01:11:26,440
I'll be back.

1272
01:11:27,386 --> 01:11:29,456
Everything is normal.

1273
01:11:29,536 --> 01:11:30,971
- Thank God.
- These minor pains

1274
01:11:31,051 --> 01:11:32,455
are normal during pregnancy.

1275
01:11:32,853 --> 01:11:34,339
By the way, where's the baby's father?

1276
01:11:34,419 --> 01:11:36,116
- He--
- Doctor. I am here.

1277
01:11:36,437 --> 01:11:38,165
You can see me.
I am the father.

1278
01:11:38,245 --> 01:11:40,007
Many congratulations.

1279
01:11:40,358 --> 01:11:42,743
- Thank you.
- But why have you covered your face?

1280
01:11:43,349 --> 01:11:44,551
Any worries?

1281
01:11:44,843 --> 01:11:48,233
No worries. It's a father's story.

1282
01:11:48,465 --> 01:11:53,048
Like a mother, a father also
watches his child grow for nine months.

1283
01:11:53,686 --> 01:11:55,771
He rocks him in his
arms for three years.

1284
01:11:55,851 --> 01:11:57,659
And loves him from
the bottom of his heart for a lifetime.

1285
01:11:57,739 --> 01:11:58,657
Birdie.

1286
01:11:58,891 --> 01:12:00,859
- How sweet.
- Wow.

1287
01:12:01,243 --> 01:12:04,579
These words sound familiar.

1288
01:12:04,861 --> 01:12:08,797
No, no... it's about a father's glory.

1289
01:12:09,805 --> 01:12:11,833
Sacrificing all his desires,

1290
01:12:11,913 --> 01:12:15,271
a father showers all
his love on his child.

1291
01:12:15,863 --> 01:12:16,869
What?

1292
01:12:17,333 --> 01:12:19,959
A father's love just like
a mother's affection.

1293
