Stealing in your own house?

1681
01:32:17,242 --> 01:32:18,034
Yes, I am.

1682
01:32:19,284 --> 01:32:20,826
Preet should also get these.

1683
01:32:21,159 --> 01:32:23,201
For her health and
the growth of her child.

1684
01:32:24,784 --> 01:32:26,577
I can't share my mother's love,

1685
01:32:27,095 --> 01:32:28,727
but I can share these sweets with her.

1686
01:32:30,576 --> 01:32:31,784
Let me help you.

1687
01:32:33,650 --> 01:32:34,909
Are you pregnant?

1688
01:32:35,617 --> 01:32:37,451
What about my growth?

1689
01:32:38,642 --> 01:32:39,659
They're for my children.

1690
01:32:39,930 --> 01:32:41,037
- Let me have one.
- Go take steroids.

1691
01:32:41,117 --> 01:32:42,278
- At least leave the jar behind.
- Get lost.

1692
01:32:42,601 --> 01:32:44,201
Sweets made of
dry fruit and fenugreek.

1693
01:32:44,549 --> 01:32:46,826
My mom sent these
from Punjab for Preet.

1694
01:32:47,159 --> 01:32:49,867
For the health of the
mother and growth of our baby.

1695
01:32:49,951 --> 01:32:51,951
How nice of them, right, Preet ma'am?

1696
01:32:52,034 --> 01:32:56,492
Brother... if Mom was alive,
she would've done this for me.

1697
01:32:57,242 --> 01:33:00,034
Preet. My mother is like your mother.

1698
01:33:00,492 --> 01:33:04,730
Excellent, Jass.
You said such a lovely thing.

1699
01:33:05,932 --> 01:33:07,826
In that case, call her here.

1700
01:33:08,284 --> 01:33:10,148
- Whom?
- Your mother.

1701
01:33:11,201 --> 01:33:13,617
- What an idea? Right?
- Guggi.

1702
01:33:13,697 --> 01:33:16,367
- Sire.
- Get his mother... a ticket.

1703
01:33:16,451 --> 01:33:18,159
- Yes.
- Thank you, brother.

1704
01:33:18,242 --> 01:33:21,367
Stop talking... about my mother.

1705
01:33:22,159 --> 01:33:23,326
Mom can't come here.

1706
01:33:23,572 --> 01:33:25,034
- Why?
- Why?

1707
01:33:26,377 --> 01:33:29,242
We were born poor.
So, Mom looks after the house.

1708
01:33:30,242 --> 01:33:31,659
- Guggi.
- Yes, sire?

1709
01:33:32,242 --> 01:33:34,996
Send a few servants to his house.

1710
01:33:35,076 --> 01:33:36,742
There are many court
cases against Mom.

1711
01:33:36,826 --> 01:33:37,617
- She's a default--
- Guggi.

1712
01:33:37,701 --> 01:33:39,867
- Sire?
- Send a dozen lawyers as well.

1713
01:33:39,951 --> 01:33:41,742
- Sire.
- Anything else?

1714
01:33:41,826 --> 01:33:43,326
Our relatives...

1715
01:33:43,409 --> 01:33:46,208
We're not on good
terms with our relatives.

1716
01:33:46,784 --> 01:33:49,617
If Mom comes here,
they'll take over our land.

1717
01:33:49,826 --> 01:33:51,451
Should we send a dozen shooters?

1718
01:33:51,534 --> 01:33:52,867
Shooters?

1719
01:33:54,034 --> 01:33:56,617
- Shooters?
- No relatives, no fight.

1720
01:33:56,701 --> 01:33:58,117
- Brother.
- Anything else?

1721
01:34:00,971 --> 01:34:03,576
Hey, what happened, baby?

1722
01:34:04,117 --> 01:34:07,576
Everyone's talking about my mom,
but no one's asked about my dad.

1723
01:34:07,826 --> 01:34:09,992
My mom won't leave my dad alone
and come here.

1724
01:34:10,076 --> 01:34:12,534
- Dad...
- I understand baby, don't cry. Sit down.

1725
01:34:12,614 --> 01:34:14,451
That house is full of Dad's memories.

1726
01:34:15,251 --> 01:34:16,402
Mom can't come here
leaving them behind.

1727
01:34:16,482 --> 01:34:18,076
- Yeah, it's okay.
- No chance.

1728
01:34:20,076 --> 01:34:21,284
- Guggi...
- Sire?

1729
01:34:21,367 --> 01:34:23,659
- Book a chartered flight to India.
- Yes, sire.

1730
01:34:23,826 --> 01:34:25,565
Because we're going home,

1731
01:34:26,267 --> 01:34:29,689
to our motherland
and Jass' mother.

1732
01:34:29,867 --> 01:34:32,492
Amazing idea, brother.
You're the best.

1733
01:34:32,576 --> 01:34:34,367
Thank you so much.

1734
01:34:35,284 --> 01:34:38,867
You are so stubborn...
So stubborn.

1735
01:34:38,951 --> 01:34:42,451
You're really stubborn.
You just don't give up.

1736
01:34:42,742 --> 01:34:45,326
Instead of all of us going there,
Mom will come here.

1737
01:34:45,617 --> 01:34:46,909
My mom will come here.

1738
01:34:48,893 --> 01:34:50,662
"Toasted. Toasted. Toasted."

1739
01:34:50,742 --> 01:34:52,576
Kunnu. You called at the right time.

1740
01:34:52,659 --> 01:34:53,492
Why? What happened, Jass?

1741
01:34:53,576 --> 01:34:54,951
Randhawa wants to meet Mom.

1742
01:34:55,034 --> 01:34:57,409
Great. Serves you right for
stuffing her with mom's sweets.

1743
01:34:58,034 --> 01:34:59,117
- Sir, sugar?
- Leave.

1744
01:34:59,201 --> 01:35:01,617
- Okay, sir.
- How do I introduce them to Mom?

1745
01:35:01,797 --> 01:35:03,037
And where am I supposed
to find a fake mother?

1746
01:35:03,117 --> 01:35:05,117
Relax. Your Mom will be there.

1747
01:35:05,201 --> 01:35:06,617
We'll find you a mom
as good as your real mom.

1748
01:35:06,701 --> 01:35:09,617
I don't want a glimpse,
I want a full grown mother,

1749
01:35:09,697 --> 01:35:12,723
someone like old Nirupa Roy.

1750
01:35:14,034 --> 01:35:17,313
She'll come.
She'll come. She'll come.

1751
01:35:27,245 --> 01:35:31,506
"Mom... my dear Mom..."

1752
01:35:31,648 --> 01:35:35,256
"You're my darling child."

1753
01:35:37,423 --> 01:35:41,673
"Mom... my dear Mom..."

1754
01:35:41,756 --> 01:35:45,590
"You're my darling child."

1755
01:35:49,581 --> 01:35:52,994
Sire, isn't she too
young to be his mother?

1756
01:35:54,839 --> 01:35:57,781
You asked for a mother...
and my mom's here.

1757
01:35:58,833 --> 01:36:02,125
Excellent. Delhi is for those
with a big heart, and London--

1758
01:36:02,333 --> 01:36:04,250
Let it be, Mom. Let it be.

1759
01:36:05,791 --> 01:36:10,250
Hello, Mr. Randhawa.
I got something for you.

1760
01:36:10,875 --> 01:36:12,875
You feel cold at night, don't you?

1761
01:36:12,958 --> 01:36:14,791
- A sweater, for you.
- How nice.

1762
01:36:14,875 --> 01:36:16,333
It will keep you warm.

1763
01:36:17,083 --> 01:36:19,333
- Thank you.
- Why are you standing at the back?

1764
01:36:19,750 --> 01:36:21,083
- You're his servant, aren't you?
- He is.

1765
01:36:21,583 --> 01:36:22,666
I can tell.

1766
01:36:23,083 --> 01:36:25,167
- Preet, my daughter-in-law.
- Hello, Mom.

1767
01:36:26,916 --> 01:36:28,666
This is for you.

1768
01:36:29,041 --> 01:36:30,750
- A picture of little Jass.
- Aww.

1769
01:36:30,833 --> 01:36:32,125
So cute.

1770
01:36:32,208 --> 01:36:34,541
- Alice, this dress is for you.
- Thank you.

1771
01:36:34,625 --> 01:36:36,541
I heard you take good
care of my daughter-in-law.

1772
01:36:36,625 --> 01:36:40,000
Strange. You know
everything about everyone.

1773
01:36:40,666 --> 01:36:43,875
She is my mother and
mothers know everything.

1774
01:36:43,958 --> 01:36:44,916
Right, brother?

1775
01:36:45,500 --> 01:36:48,083
Come, Mom. We'll continue
this conversation inside.

1776
01:36:48,793 --> 01:36:49,295
Let's go.

1777
01:36:49,375 --> 01:36:50,250
- Come.
- Let's go.

1778
01:36:50,333 --> 01:36:51,208
Brother, come.

1779
01:36:51,291 --> 01:36:53,864
How is your mother so young?

1780
01:36:53,944 --> 01:36:55,883
Shut up, Alice's lover.

1781
01:36:55,963 --> 01:36:58,699
Don't ask too many questions.
Even I have answers.

1782
01:36:58,779 --> 01:37:01,000
Sire. Sire. Sire.
Get lost.

1783
01:37:03,166 --> 01:37:05,479
He knows about my affair.

1784
01:37:05,948 --> 01:37:08,799
Mr. Kunnu, it's good to
have you back alone.

1785
01:37:08,936 --> 01:37:10,241
Did your psychotic friend leave UK--

1786
01:37:10,321 --> 01:37:13,125
What did I say? What did I bloody say?

1787
01:37:13,275 --> 01:37:15,947
I asked for someone mature,
like Nirupa Roy.

1788
01:37:16,071 --> 01:37:17,532
You sent me Mouni Roy.

1789
01:37:17,824 --> 01:37:18,741
So young!

1790
01:37:18,824 --> 01:37:21,282
Even Shah Rukh Khan
wasn't this young in 'Jawan'.

1791
01:37:21,532 --> 01:37:22,911
Sorry, Jass.

1792
01:37:22,991 --> 01:37:25,491
This was the best I could arrange
at such short notice.

1793
01:37:26,574 --> 01:37:29,657
But I'm sure she handled
everything perfectly, right?

1794
01:37:29,741 --> 01:37:31,347
Handled? Nonsense.

1795
01:37:31,427 --> 01:37:32,449
She walked in and said

1796
01:37:32,532 --> 01:37:34,032
"Delhi is for those with a big heart,
and London is for--"

1797
01:37:34,116 --> 01:37:36,580
I get it. I get it. Sorry.

1798
01:37:37,636 --> 01:37:40,991
- What if I'd got caught?
- Relax, Jass.

1799
01:37:41,701 --> 01:37:43,366
She's a professional.

1800
01:37:44,366 --> 01:37:48,741
Your fake mother will never be exposed.

1801
01:37:48,824 --> 01:37:50,639
- Really?
- No one.

1802
01:37:50,719 --> 01:37:53,241
- You sure?
- No one will catch on.

1803
01:38:01,482 --> 01:38:02,804
Hold on.

1804
01:38:03,991 --> 01:38:07,616
Sire, the "mother" Jass brought here...
isn't a mother.

1805
01:38:07,949 --> 01:38:09,601
She is an incredible person.

1806
01:38:23,543 --> 01:38:28,643
"Bhaiyyaji is never late..."

1807
01:38:30,968 --> 01:38:38,241
"Bhaiyyaji is never late,
to feed his wife and tuck her in..."

1808
01:38:38,324 --> 01:38:45,673
"And keeps the neighbour's
wife awake till morning."

1809
01:38:45,753 --> 01:38:53,090
"And keeps the neighbour's
wife awake till morning."

1810
01:38:53,170 --> 01:39:00,350
"Tiptoes so she doesn't awake--"

1811
01:39:01,532 --> 01:39:03,991
She's popularly known
as Rasmalai Rajjo.

1812
01:39:04,407 --> 01:39:07,782
She has an entire series
of vulgar songs with weird names.

1813
01:39:07,862 --> 01:39:14,373
"And keeps the neighbour's
wife awake till morning."

1814
01:39:14,991 --> 01:39:19,032
Dilphek Doodhwali,
Makkhan Malishwali, Chikni Chupdi...

1815
01:39:20,782 --> 01:39:22,619
"...awake till morning."

1816
01:39:23,907 --> 01:39:25,866
My judgment was severely impaired.

1817
01:39:27,032 --> 01:39:30,116
Mistaking coal for a diamond...
and mud for a lotus.

1818
01:39:32,282 --> 01:39:34,199
Speak up, Jass's respected mother.

1819
01:39:35,074 --> 01:39:37,532
How do you explain this vulgarity?

1820
01:39:39,781 --> 01:39:42,852
All I want to say is...

1821
01:39:43,175 --> 01:39:44,157
I am not Jass's mother.

1822
01:39:44,564 --> 01:39:45,516
Sire!

1823
01:39:46,324 --> 01:39:49,353
Jass? What is Mom saying?

1824
01:39:50,116 --> 01:39:54,032
Jass will clarify
whatever needs clarifying.

1825
01:39:55,116 --> 01:39:58,741
- Jass!
- Yes, it's true. She's not my mother.

1826
01:39:59,032 --> 01:40:01,782
But before you pull out the gun,
hear me out first.

1827
01:40:01,866 --> 01:40:03,241
What is the entire story?

1828
01:40:04,491 --> 01:40:06,616
- Let me speak.
- Speak.

1829
01:40:07,157 --> 01:40:09,991
This goes back to when I was a child.

1830
01:40:10,074 --> 01:40:11,157
A small boy.

1831
01:40:11,491 --> 01:40:16,241
My real mother, Paramjeet, had a younger
sister Sharamjeet... aka Shammo.

1832
01:40:16,491 --> 01:40:17,532
This lady.

1833
01:40:17,782 --> 01:40:20,699
She was having an affair
with a guy called Shammi at that time.

1834
01:40:21,366 --> 01:40:24,784
When my mother found out
her sister was getting married,

1835
01:40:24,864 --> 01:40:27,199
she was overjoyed...
singing, dancing...

1836
01:40:33,991 --> 01:40:35,032
Do you know what was behind her?

1837
01:40:35,116 --> 01:40:36,991
Normally people talk about
what happened ahead.

1838
01:40:37,074 --> 01:40:38,616
Yes, but in this story,
what was behind her is more important.

1839
01:40:38,824 --> 01:40:40,657
While my mother was singing and dancing,

1840
01:40:40,824 --> 01:40:42,532
there was a long staircase behind her.

1841
01:40:42,616 --> 01:40:43,911
She slipped and fell--

1842
01:40:43,991 --> 01:40:47,105
Thud... thud... thud...
thud... thud... thud...

1843
01:40:47,185 --> 01:40:48,186
Next.

1844
01:40:48,741 --> 01:40:49,907
It was a long staircase. Hold on.

1845
01:40:50,271 --> 01:40:52,782
Thud... thud... thud...
thud... thud... thud...

1846
01:40:53,116 --> 01:40:53,991
Is she down yet?

1847
01:40:54,074 --> 01:40:56,241
No, my mother went up,
straight up to heaven.

1848
01:40:57,366 --> 01:40:59,241
I was very emotionally fragile.

1849
01:41:00,032 --> 01:41:04,366
I went to my aunt and said,
"Aunty, will you marry my dad?"

1850
01:41:04,449 --> 01:41:06,241
"Will you love this
child like his own mom?"

1851
01:41:07,032 --> 01:41:10,657
And without hesitation,
this great woman said 'yes'.

1852
01:41:11,407 --> 01:41:12,616
Ask... Ask her.

1853
01:41:12,991 --> 01:41:14,657
Help me. Stop taking footage.

1854
01:41:14,741 --> 01:41:17,032
Yes, I said yes.

1855
01:41:17,907 --> 01:41:20,532
I said, yes I will raise this child.

1856
01:41:21,157 --> 01:41:23,170
She is not educated.
She is completely illiterate.

1857
01:41:23,250 --> 01:41:24,694
She says wrong things
at the wrong time.

1858
01:41:24,774 --> 01:41:28,782
But she has a gift...
she can dance.

1859
01:41:28,866 --> 01:41:29,699
Yes.

1860
01:41:37,449 --> 01:41:39,625
With a heavy heart...

1861
01:41:41,018 --> 01:41:43,032
and flexible moves,

1862
01:41:44,699 --> 01:41:48,865
she became Rasmalai Rajjo.

1863
01:41:51,907 --> 01:41:55,823
Made videos for Tips, T-Series, Venus,
in order to raise me.

1864
01:41:56,407 --> 01:41:59,449
You showed me four
videos, I'll show you 40.

1865
01:42:00,241 --> 01:42:01,574
'Bangkok Mein Bhauchaal'

1866
01:42:02,657 --> 01:42:03,991
'Chunari mein Lugai'

1867
01:42:04,991 --> 01:42:06,366
'Ghagre Mein WiFi'

1868
01:42:11,157 --> 01:42:12,574
'Lollipop Lugai...'

1869
01:42:12,824 --> 01:42:14,324
'Choli ke Peeche Toli'

1870
01:42:14,407 --> 01:42:15,866
'Aunty Ke Peeche Bunty'

1871
01:42:15,949 --> 01:42:17,089
Enough!

1872
01:42:19,322 --> 01:42:20,311
Mom...

1873
01:42:22,073 --> 01:42:23,387
It's okay.

1874
01:42:23,987 --> 01:42:24,907
Wow!

1875
01:42:26,407 --> 01:42:27,599
Very touching, sir.

1876
01:42:30,282 --> 01:42:32,211
Please forgive me, Ms. Sharamjeet.

1877
01:42:33,657 --> 01:42:35,574
I misjudged you.

1878
01:42:36,565 --> 01:42:38,616
You turned out to be a goddess.

1879
01:42:40,241 --> 01:42:41,866
Epitome of motherhood.

1880
01:42:42,199 --> 01:42:47,532
What I did... wasn't by choice.

1881
01:42:48,378 --> 01:42:51,407
It was a single mother's helplessness.

1882
01:42:51,991 --> 01:42:53,327
Forgive me.

1883
01:43:08,179 --> 01:43:11,807
"It happens in this age,"

1884
01:43:11,887 --> 01:43:15,652
"You lose sleep and peace."

1885
01:43:15,732 --> 01:43:19,550
"It happens in this age,"

1886
01:43:19,630 --> 01:43:21,491
"You lose sleep and peace."

1887
01:43:21,782 --> 01:43:24,491
Sharamjeet, try this orange dress.

1888
01:43:25,738 --> 01:43:28,032
It will suit you.

1889
01:43:28,907 --> 01:43:30,935
And this lime colour...

1890
01:43:32,530 --> 01:43:34,108
will look even better on you.

1891
01:43:34,366 --> 01:43:36,616
But, Mr. Randhawa,
how can I accept all this?

1892
01:43:37,454 --> 01:43:39,449
And this white...

1893
01:43:40,532 --> 01:43:42,286
Marvellous.

1894
01:43:42,626 --> 01:43:45,918
This colour will look vibrant on you.

1895
01:43:48,657 --> 01:43:50,740
Shammo ji, so many dresses?

1896
01:43:50,820 --> 01:43:52,311
Are you taking them
to the laundry?

1897
01:43:52,491 --> 01:43:54,699
Mr. Randhawa told me try these on.

1898
01:43:55,027 --> 01:43:56,961
He personally chose them for me.

1899
01:43:59,407 --> 01:44:02,866
Brother-in-law.
Your mother is robbing my boss.

1900
01:44:02,949 --> 01:44:04,914
Why are you getting so irritated?

1901
01:44:09,825 --> 01:44:10,821
"Mom..."

1902
01:44:11,949 --> 01:44:12,782
Wow...

1903
01:44:13,805 --> 01:44:14,657
Mom?

1904
01:44:17,866 --> 01:44:20,032
"Mom... my dear Mom..."

1905
01:44:20,116 --> 01:44:23,616
- Mom!
- "You're my darling child."

1906
01:44:24,366 --> 01:44:26,981
- "I'm your darling child."
- Oh Mom!

1907
01:44:47,366 --> 01:44:49,911
Jass, just look at this. So cute, right?

1908
01:44:49,991 --> 01:44:51,691
Which one should we buy?
Blue or pink?

1909
01:44:54,671 --> 01:44:57,449
My dear wife, let's ask the
one who's going to wear it.

1910
01:44:57,824 --> 01:45:00,616
Junior, if you mind,
can I ask you something?

1911
01:45:00,991 --> 01:45:02,093
Which colour...

1912
01:45:07,532 --> 01:45:09,991
Excuse me. Baby product?

1913
01:45:10,140 --> 01:45:11,574
For my baby.

1914
01:45:12,074 --> 01:45:15,361
Everyone in London is becoming a father.

1915
01:45:23,074 --> 01:45:25,366
Brother-in-law? You here?

1916
01:45:25,449 --> 01:45:27,324
For my baby. Preet's baby.

1917
01:45:27,699 --> 01:45:30,407
Forget about me.
What are you doing here?

1918
01:45:30,491 --> 01:45:32,241
I was just...

1919
01:45:32,574 --> 01:45:33,949
My Guggudu...

1920
01:45:34,199 --> 01:45:35,696
Alice in Guggiland.

1921
01:45:36,741 --> 01:45:38,532
Alice is just my love...

1922
01:45:38,699 --> 01:45:42,532
Love may not satisfy hunger,
but it definitely leads to a baby bump.

1923
01:45:42,616 --> 01:45:45,157
And you can't control a horny.

1924
01:45:45,241 --> 01:45:46,574
Shall we give the good
news to Randhawa sir?

1925
01:45:46,657 --> 01:45:48,241
- No, no...
- No, I'll tell him.

1926
01:45:48,324 --> 01:45:49,491
- Brother-in-law...
- No, no...

1927
01:45:49,699 --> 01:45:51,074
let's keep this a secret.

1928
01:45:51,157 --> 01:45:53,616
Then pay my bill along with yours.

1929
01:45:53,699 --> 01:45:54,741
Done.

1930
01:45:54,947 --> 01:45:56,949
- I need this.
- Done.

1931
01:45:58,350 --> 01:45:59,559
Wet wipes.

1932
01:46:02,991 --> 01:46:06,067
But, Mr. Randhawa,
how can I accept this?

1933
01:46:06,324 --> 01:46:07,782
I am Jass's mother.

1934
01:46:09,824 --> 01:46:14,139
You did not give birth to Jass,
only raised him.

1935
01:46:16,657 --> 01:46:17,616
Shammo...

1936
01:46:22,124 --> 01:46:25,364
24-karat indium gold!

1937
01:46:32,075 --> 01:46:33,532
Guggi, why did she leave like this?

1938
01:46:34,157 --> 01:46:35,782
It's called values, boss.

1939
01:46:36,116 --> 01:46:37,732
No matter how mature a girl becomes,

1940
01:46:38,157 --> 01:46:39,911
whenever the topic
of her marriage comes up,

1941
01:46:39,991 --> 01:46:43,121
she gets embarrassed and runs away.

1942
01:46:44,241 --> 01:46:46,241
Sharamjeet,
what's going on in this house?

1943
01:46:46,324 --> 01:46:47,199
Do you know they--

1944
01:46:51,282 --> 01:46:52,875
Did Mr. Randhawa give you this?

1945
01:46:55,487 --> 01:46:56,578
It's a pre-wedding gift.

1946
01:46:58,907 --> 01:47:02,699
Son, I'm the mistress of this house now.

1947
01:47:03,282 --> 01:47:06,824
I'll do as I please, mister.

1948
01:47:06,949 --> 01:47:09,157
Preet. Preet. Control your brother.

1949
01:47:09,241 --> 01:47:10,866
He wants to marry my mother.

1950
01:47:10,949 --> 01:47:12,282
- Jass...
- What is he doing?

1951
01:47:12,449 --> 01:47:13,657
Jass, listen...

1952
01:47:13,741 --> 01:47:15,491
That's what I said. "Brother, listen".

1953
01:47:15,616 --> 01:47:17,157
After the marriage,
what will you call her?

1954
01:47:17,241 --> 01:47:18,407
Mother-in-law or sister-in-law?

1955
01:47:18,491 --> 01:47:21,116
And what are the kids going to call her?
Grandma or Aunty?

1956
01:47:21,199 --> 01:47:22,699
This will become that,
that will become this.

1957
01:47:22,782 --> 01:47:24,449
It will become a cocktail
of relationships.

1958
01:47:24,532 --> 01:47:25,824
Jass, listen to me.

1959
01:47:25,907 --> 01:47:28,199
At his age, he should
be blessings newly weds,

1960
01:47:28,366 --> 01:47:29,366
not planning his own wedding.

1961
01:47:29,449 --> 01:47:31,617
Jass, goddamnit, listen to me!

1962
01:47:32,157 --> 01:47:34,116
My water just broke.

1963
01:47:34,199 --> 01:47:36,074
This baby is coming now!

1964
01:47:40,181 --> 01:47:41,866
- Oh my God.
- Doctor. Call the doctor.

1965
01:47:41,949 --> 01:47:42,952
We need a doctor.

1966
01:47:43,032 --> 01:47:44,074
Calm down, baby. Calm down.

1967
01:47:44,605 --> 01:47:46,172
- Move.
- Oh my God.

1968
01:47:46,252 --> 01:47:47,319
Calm down, baby. Calm down.

1969
01:47:47,461 --> 01:47:49,324
Don't tell me to calm down!

1970
01:47:49,407 --> 01:47:51,241
- Okay.
- This is your fault.

1971
01:47:51,324 --> 01:47:53,491
- Sorry. I am sorry.
- Where are we going?

1972
01:47:53,574 --> 01:47:54,574
Fast.

1973
01:47:57,032 --> 01:47:59,911
Doctor, how can her water break
at just seven and a half months?

1974
01:47:59,991 --> 01:48:02,911
Wow, what a concerned father.

1975
01:48:02,991 --> 01:48:04,366
He takes such good care of her.

1976
01:48:04,449 --> 01:48:05,407
- Doctor.
- Yes, my dear?

1977
01:48:05,491 --> 01:48:06,866
What about me and the baby?

1978
01:48:06,949 --> 01:48:08,741
Don't worry.
I'll give you a painkiller.

1979
01:48:08,824 --> 01:48:11,616
I've got everything under control.
Please, everyone go out.

1980
01:48:11,699 --> 01:48:13,366
- I don't like overcrowded wards, please.
- Doctor?

1981
01:48:13,449 --> 01:48:14,657
- Yes, my dear?
- Can I please stay here?

1982
01:48:14,741 --> 01:48:15,949
- Excuse me?
- Please.

1983
01:48:16,241 --> 01:48:18,240
How are you related to her?

1984
01:48:19,699 --> 01:48:22,699
Well... I'm like her mother.

1985
01:48:23,782 --> 01:48:25,199
- Thank you.
- I'll be right back. One second.

1986
01:48:25,282 --> 01:48:26,696
Jass? Hey...

1987
01:48:28,991 --> 01:48:30,627
Why did I get four
missed calls from Mom?

1988
01:48:31,574 --> 01:48:32,491
Jass?

1989
01:48:32,991 --> 01:48:33,907
Mom?

1990
01:48:34,992 --> 01:48:36,814
I've been trying to call you.
Where've you been?

1991
01:48:37,116 --> 01:48:38,032
Why weren't you answering your phone?

1992
01:48:38,116 --> 01:48:39,952
- Mom, I was--
- Baani's labour pains have started.

1993
01:48:40,032 --> 01:48:41,241
I've brought her to the hospital.

1994
01:48:41,324 --> 01:48:42,241
Baani is here?

1995
01:48:42,324 --> 01:48:44,282
First, tell me what you are doing here?

1996
01:48:44,991 --> 01:48:49,116
I... Before I tell you my story,
tell me where Baani is.

1997
01:48:50,491 --> 01:48:52,574
- You okay?
- No!

1998
01:48:53,241 --> 01:48:55,157
- But I'm happy you're here.
- Me too.

1999
01:48:55,241 --> 01:48:57,949
Son. The doctor is saying
she can deliver today.

2000
01:48:58,032 --> 01:48:58,952
- Today?
- Yes.

2001
01:48:59,032 --> 01:49:01,984
And we must take good
care of her.

2002
01:49:02,064 --> 01:49:02,718
Yeah.

2003
01:49:03,449 --> 01:49:05,199
But you don't worry. Hold this.

2004
01:49:05,282 --> 01:49:06,827
Lord Ganesha will always be with us.

2005
01:49:06,907 --> 01:49:08,866
- And give me this phone.
- Give me back my phone, Mom.

2006
01:49:08,949 --> 01:49:10,491
- No. I won't...
- You did the right thing.

2007
01:49:11,939 --> 01:49:14,282
What an irresponsible father.

2008
01:49:14,741 --> 01:49:18,532
Come with me to the other room,
I'll show you a responsible father.

2009
01:49:18,616 --> 01:49:20,866
He never enters the room without a mask.

2010
01:49:21,199 --> 01:49:23,199
And look at him... terrible.

2011
01:49:23,824 --> 01:49:26,907
- He treats foreigners.
- Stop disturbing my patients and leave.

2012
01:49:27,241 --> 01:49:28,202
- Jass.
- Baani, I'll be right back.

2013
01:49:28,282 --> 01:49:29,116
Mom, my phone.

2014
01:49:29,199 --> 01:49:30,907
- Give it.
- Out. Out.

2015
01:49:32,199 --> 01:49:34,157
- Why doesn't he ever answer his phone?
- Again?

2016
01:49:34,907 --> 01:49:36,010
Why is everyone calling me?

2017
01:49:36,090 --> 01:49:38,282
- Where were you?
- I...was...

2018
01:49:38,532 --> 01:49:39,718
I've been calling for so long.

2019
01:49:40,074 --> 01:49:40,782
Not working.

2020
01:49:40,866 --> 01:49:43,199
The doctors are saying they'll
have to do a premature delivery,

2021
01:49:43,282 --> 01:49:44,324
and it has to be done today.

2022
01:49:45,574 --> 01:49:46,952
Today? Both of them?

2023
01:49:47,032 --> 01:49:48,098
What do you mean both of them?

2024
01:49:48,366 --> 01:49:49,407
Is there someone else?

2025
01:49:50,449 --> 01:49:56,074
When... a child is born,
a mother is also born.

2026
01:49:56,241 --> 01:49:57,157
So both.

2027
01:49:57,657 --> 01:49:59,782
Great. He's absolutely right.

2028
01:50:00,032 --> 01:50:00,866
The doctor's here.

2029
01:50:00,949 --> 01:50:01,866
Oh no.

2030
01:50:01,949 --> 01:50:06,699
Doctor, tell him about
Preet's premature delivery.

2031
01:50:07,574 --> 01:50:08,972
Why should I tell him?

2032
01:50:09,574 --> 01:50:12,157
Because he's the child's father.

2033
01:50:14,324 --> 01:50:17,032
He's the father of this child?

2034
01:50:17,616 --> 01:50:20,616
- Are you sure?
- Of course he is.

2035
01:50:21,157 --> 01:50:23,491
You must have seen him in a mask.

2036
01:50:23,574 --> 01:50:25,949
Look closely. Recognise him?

2037
01:50:27,574 --> 01:50:29,324
Same-same. I know him.

2038
01:50:29,407 --> 01:50:30,616
- Father and doctor have to talk.
- I recognise him.

2039
01:50:30,699 --> 01:50:32,692
- Father and doctor.
- Aren't you the same guy?

2040
01:50:32,772 --> 01:50:33,866
What did you say?

2041
01:50:34,366 --> 01:50:38,640
"Who's Your Daddy? Jumping with joy?"
I'll tell them everything.

2042
01:50:38,782 --> 01:50:40,532
- Mr. Randhawa...
- Dr. Gulati, emergency.

2043
01:50:40,616 --> 01:50:42,449
- What happened?
- Your patient is about to die.

2044
01:50:42,532 --> 01:50:43,991
- Hurry up or he will die.
- I'm coming back.

2045
01:50:44,074 --> 01:50:46,911
- I'm coming back. I'm coming back.
- We can't deliver a baby without a doctor.

2046
01:50:46,991 --> 01:50:48,199
I'm coming back.

2047
01:50:48,670 --> 01:50:50,282
Watch out. Hurry up.

2048
01:50:50,366 --> 01:50:52,241
How can I hurry up
when I'm sitting down?

2049
01:50:52,324 --> 01:50:53,616
Then hurry up while sitting down.

2050
01:50:55,782 --> 01:50:57,157
Where's the patient?

2051
01:50:58,158 --> 01:51:00,366
- Where's the patient?
- There is no patient, sir.

2052
01:51:00,782 --> 01:51:02,574
I lied to you.

2053
01:51:03,157 --> 01:51:05,952
- Because I had to tell you the truth.
- What truth?

2054
01:51:06,032 --> 01:51:07,421
Actually--

2055
01:51:07,741 --> 01:51:09,528
His truth.

2056
01:51:09,782 --> 01:51:11,620
He's not a bad guy,

2057
01:51:11,863 --> 01:51:14,241
he just kept getting stuck
in bad situations.

2058
01:51:14,324 --> 01:51:17,696
Selfie Kumar, he has two wives.

2059
01:51:17,991 --> 01:51:19,866
He's expecting two children.

2060
01:51:20,032 --> 01:51:21,365
It's a crime!

2061
01:51:21,824 --> 01:51:24,241
Doctor, Baani and Preet are in labour.

2062
01:51:24,491 --> 01:51:26,699
Preet will undergo a premature delivery.

2063
01:51:26,782 --> 01:51:27,869
I will tell them the truth,

2064
01:51:27,949 --> 01:51:29,282
but after the delivery is done.

2065
01:51:29,366 --> 01:51:33,116
I will deliver... you... to jail.

2066
01:51:33,282 --> 01:51:35,657
- I am going to expose this fraud!
- Please, doctor.

2067
01:51:35,741 --> 01:51:36,622
Out of my way--

2068
01:51:36,702 --> 01:51:37,869
Doctor, I cannot give
stress to both mothers.

2069
01:51:37,949 --> 01:51:38,952
- Move!
- Gulati.

2070
01:51:41,616 --> 01:51:46,491
Before you go out,
take a look at your own dirty deeds.

2071
01:51:46,741 --> 01:51:47,490
Look.

2072
01:51:47,657 --> 01:51:50,819
"Look aunt,
your boy's going astray."

2073
01:51:50,991 --> 01:51:54,674
"Look aunt,
your boy's going astray."

2074
01:51:54,754 --> 01:51:58,853
"Look aunt,
your boy's going astray."

2075
01:52:01,949 --> 01:52:05,283
"Look aunt,
your boy's going astray."

2076
01:52:05,633 --> 01:52:09,199
"Stop teasing girls."

2077
01:52:09,282 --> 01:52:12,805
"I'll report you,
I'll get you arrested."

2078
01:52:12,980 --> 01:52:15,011
"I'll get you thrown in jail."

2079
01:52:15,091 --> 01:52:18,636
"Stop teasing girls."

2080
01:52:20,991 --> 01:52:22,741
Fake university doctor, get up.

2081
01:52:22,824 --> 01:52:24,901
Godamba! Godamba!

2082
01:52:25,144 --> 01:52:27,241
Doctor, which brand
of cheap tobacco is this?

2083
01:52:27,324 --> 01:52:28,866
Godamba is my wife's name.

2084
01:52:28,949 --> 01:52:30,824
If she finds out,
she'll beat me to a pulp.

2085
01:52:30,907 --> 01:52:33,116
I am married. I have two kids, please.

2086
01:52:33,199 --> 01:52:35,968
- And, even I am expecting babies.
- Two of them.

2087
01:52:36,574 --> 01:52:38,407
- You like reading books, don't you?
- Yes.

2088
01:52:38,491 --> 01:52:40,116
- Then you should read another book.
- Which one?

2089
01:52:40,199 --> 01:52:43,407
'Zindagi Jhandba Toh Muh Humesha Band Ba'
(When Life's A Train Wreck, You Better Zip It)

2090
01:52:44,324 --> 01:52:46,532
Otherwise you will become a widower.

2091
01:52:46,616 --> 01:52:47,991
Delivery. Please.

2092
01:52:48,491 --> 01:52:50,824
Breathe. Breathe.

2093
01:52:50,907 --> 01:52:53,032
Check where he is. Call him.

2094
01:52:53,116 --> 01:52:53,816
Give me your hand.

2095
01:52:53,896 --> 01:52:56,491
Call my husband. Out of the way.

2096
01:52:56,574 --> 01:52:57,977
Out of the way.

2097
01:53:00,157 --> 01:53:02,491
Lord Ganesha, first Baani came
in my life and then she left.

2098
01:53:02,657 --> 01:53:04,449
Then Preet came and so did Baani.

2099
01:53:04,907 --> 01:53:08,199
Lord Ganesha,
protect the mothers and the children.

2100
01:53:08,282 --> 01:53:09,366
Lord...

2101
01:53:10,116 --> 01:53:11,396
Who are you talking to, man?

2102
01:53:12,116 --> 01:53:14,199
Indian emotion. You won't understand.

2103
01:53:14,491 --> 01:53:15,991
I'm in deep trouble. Deep.

2104
01:53:18,847 --> 01:53:21,241
- Come on, push, push. You can do it.
- Jass, don't touch me.

2105
01:53:21,324 --> 01:53:23,787
- It's all because of you.
- Okay, sorry. Push, push.

2106
01:53:23,867 --> 01:53:25,032
You can do it.
You can do it.

2107
01:53:25,116 --> 01:53:27,282
Hallelujah, the baby's on its way.

2108
01:53:27,366 --> 01:53:28,699
It's a big baby.

2109
01:53:28,782 --> 01:53:30,782
I've got to check before I take it out.

2110
01:53:30,866 --> 01:53:34,199
- It's coming. It's coming.
- Hurry up.

2111
01:53:34,983 --> 01:53:36,393
Hurry up!

2112
01:53:46,241 --> 01:53:48,941
Congratulations, it's a girl.

2113
01:53:50,116 --> 01:53:53,574
With God's blessings,
I'm finally a grandma.

2114
01:53:54,824 --> 01:53:57,032
I had decided that if all went well,

2115
01:53:57,532 --> 01:53:59,824
I will go to Vaishno Devi
to seek blessings.

2116
01:53:59,991 --> 01:54:00,933
Mom...

2117
01:54:02,782 --> 01:54:05,241
Godamba. Godamba. Godamba.

2118
01:54:05,657 --> 01:54:09,032
Congratulations.
This time it's a boy.

2119
01:54:09,116 --> 01:54:10,911
- So sorry.
- Great.

2120
01:54:10,991 --> 01:54:12,116
Remember I told you, brother.

2121
01:54:12,199 --> 01:54:15,032
Uncle and nephew
swaying all over London.

2122
01:54:15,116 --> 01:54:16,657
Spinning... Spinning...

2123
01:54:16,741 --> 01:54:19,574
- Little Randhawa is here--
- What are you doing, Mr. Randhawa?

2124
01:54:19,657 --> 01:54:20,614
It's a hospital.

2125
01:54:21,116 --> 01:54:22,143
- Hold your gun.
- Brother.

2126
01:54:22,223 --> 01:54:23,114
Yes.

2127
01:54:26,116 --> 01:54:27,616
Even he looks like me.

2128
01:54:27,699 --> 01:54:29,271
I mean, only he looks like me.

2129
01:54:31,657 --> 01:54:32,949
Thank you again.

2130
01:54:33,032 --> 01:54:34,366
There's only two, right?

2131
01:54:42,722 --> 01:54:43,898
We'll go to India soon.

2132
01:54:44,444 --> 01:54:46,055
Jass, Mom and the baby
are in the parking lot, right?

2133
01:54:46,135 --> 01:54:47,219
Yes.

2134
01:54:48,427 --> 01:54:49,802
- Baani...
- What?

2135
01:54:49,885 --> 01:54:51,023
I forgot the files.

2136
01:54:51,353 --> 01:54:52,339
Call the elevator, I'll get them.

2137
01:54:52,419 --> 01:54:53,510
- Okay.
- Okay.

2138
01:55:01,152 --> 01:55:03,844
- Preet?
- Baani. Hi.

2139
01:55:04,274 --> 01:55:05,649
- How are you?
- Good. You delivered?

2140
01:55:05,733 --> 01:55:08,941
- Yes, baby girl. And you?
- Baby boy.

2141
01:55:09,066 --> 01:55:11,358
- Congratulations.
- Congratulations to us.

2142
01:55:11,441 --> 01:55:13,608
- Lovely.
- Brother, my friend Baani.

2143
01:55:13,691 --> 01:55:14,566
- Nice to meet you.
- Hello.

2144
01:55:14,691 --> 01:55:17,191
- Hello.
- Preet, my husband's coming.

2145
01:55:17,274 --> 01:55:18,649
- Just two minutes.
- Okay. Nice.

2146
01:55:18,733 --> 01:55:19,983
Now Preet isn't answering her phone.

2147
01:55:20,066 --> 01:55:22,108
- She will. Keep calling.
- And she complains I'm always busy.

2148
01:55:22,649 --> 01:55:23,859
Nothing you do is ever enough for them.

2149
01:55:23,939 --> 01:55:25,066
- Same story with me.
- Yes, Mom.

2150
01:55:25,441 --> 01:55:26,899
I'm coming. Baani's already downstairs.

2151
01:55:37,816 --> 01:55:39,358
Preet, that's my husband.

2152
01:55:39,441 --> 01:55:40,733
The father of my child.

2153
01:55:52,941 --> 01:55:54,816
Baani, you're joking, right?

2154
01:55:55,149 --> 01:55:56,483
He's the father of my child.

2155
01:56:00,858 --> 01:56:04,266
No, you are joking.
He's the father of my child.

2156
01:56:04,346 --> 01:56:06,649
No, no, he's the father of my child.

2157
01:56:11,899 --> 01:56:13,191
- Are you serious?
- Yeah.

2158
01:56:13,274 --> 01:56:14,524
- What?
- What?

2159
01:56:14,941 --> 01:56:17,816
- Jass.
- Sire, do the honours.

2160
01:56:20,066 --> 01:56:22,028
Just a second,
Mr. Randhawa, I can explain.

2161
01:56:22,108 --> 01:56:24,963
- Actually by mistake--
- Rascal, what were you saying?

2162
01:56:25,441 --> 01:56:26,649
Growing love.

2163
01:56:26,888 --> 01:56:28,305
- Isn't that what he said?
- Yes.

2164
01:56:28,385 --> 01:56:29,444
No.

2165
01:56:29,524 --> 01:56:30,816
- What else did he say?
- I can't believe this.

2166
01:56:30,899 --> 01:56:32,816
- Nothing. What else did I say?
- Fraud.

2167
01:56:32,899 --> 01:56:34,028
- Oh yes.
- Stay away...

2168
01:56:34,108 --> 01:56:36,691
Nephew and uncle spinning in city.

2169
01:56:36,774 --> 01:56:38,399
- What else did you say?
- Sir, I thought you liked the song.

2170
01:56:38,733 --> 01:56:40,055
- What else did you say?
- Nothing.

2171
01:56:40,135 --> 01:56:42,862
Thud... Thud... Thud...

2172
01:56:43,024 --> 01:56:44,548
- Thud... Thud... Thud...
- Jass, how could you?

2173
01:56:44,628 --> 01:56:46,542
Thud... Thud... Thud...

2174
01:56:46,774 --> 01:56:48,399
You are Liar.

2175
01:56:48,632 --> 01:56:50,697
Thud... Thud... Thud...

2176
01:56:55,616 --> 01:57:00,243
Head towards the exit.
Do not take the lift.

2177
01:57:00,476 --> 01:57:03,725
Head towards the exit.
Do not take the lift.

2178
01:57:04,115 --> 01:57:05,657
Baani, are you alright?

2179
01:57:07,068 --> 01:57:10,848
Stay calm. Please make it to the
nearest exit as soon as possible.

2180
01:57:11,262 --> 01:57:15,518
Head towards the exit.
Do not take the lift.

2181
01:57:17,448 --> 01:57:18,524
Are you okay?

2182
01:57:18,983 --> 01:57:21,358
Catch that rascal.
Don't let him escape.

2183
01:57:21,441 --> 01:57:23,460
Jass. Where are you going?
I want answers.

2184
01:57:23,540 --> 01:57:25,971
- Brother, Jass is running away.
- Jass... Catch him.

2185
01:57:39,963 --> 01:57:41,966
Who will save me in this situation?

2186
01:57:45,149 --> 01:57:46,990
I'd told you not to share your notes.

2187
01:57:47,358 --> 01:57:49,316
Disha, where is Mr. Godbole?

2188
01:57:49,399 --> 01:57:50,566
He must be in the classroom.

2189
01:57:50,732 --> 01:57:51,691
Oh God.

2190
01:57:51,899 --> 01:57:54,781
When someone's stressed,
my crazy heart says...

2191
01:57:54,861 --> 01:57:58,441
Come to Godbole. Come to Godbole.

2192
01:57:58,524 --> 01:58:00,024
Mr. Godbole...

2193
01:58:00,191 --> 01:58:01,733
What happened, Jass?

2194
01:58:01,816 --> 01:58:03,691
My classmates are bullying me.

2195
01:58:04,191 --> 01:58:06,149
So, I got scared and ran away.

2196
01:58:06,524 --> 01:58:08,566
You got scared? Oh God.

2197
01:58:08,858 --> 01:58:10,191
So innocent.

2198
01:58:10,733 --> 01:58:13,441
Now listen carefully
to what Godbole has to say.

2199
01:58:13,733 --> 01:58:17,108
Do you know what Gandhiji said?

2200
01:58:17,688 --> 01:58:21,554
A person's biggest enemy is his fear.

2201
01:58:21,816 --> 01:58:24,358
And what did Mandela say?

2202
01:58:24,608 --> 01:58:29,919
[gibberish]

2203
01:58:31,210 --> 01:58:32,178
What is Godbole uncle doing?

2204
01:58:32,852 --> 01:58:36,761
[gibberish]

2205
01:58:37,108 --> 01:58:38,995
Mt. Kilimanjaro...

2206
01:58:39,566 --> 01:58:42,073
Control your fear, my friend.

2207
01:58:49,858 --> 01:58:50,941
There he is.

2208
01:58:52,983 --> 01:58:53,941
Hey...

2209
01:58:54,358 --> 01:58:55,491
Jass.

2210
01:58:57,441 --> 01:58:58,399
I'm ready.

2211
01:58:59,691 --> 01:59:00,733
Ask whatever you want.

2212
01:59:00,816 --> 01:59:02,858
- What have you done, Jass?
- How can you do this to us?

2213
01:59:02,941 --> 01:59:05,024
- You cheated on both of us.
- Yeah.

2214
01:59:05,575 --> 01:59:06,608
Wait a minute.

2215
01:59:06,816 --> 01:59:08,674
Baani, if you mind,
still can I ask you something?

2216
01:59:09,441 --> 01:59:11,858
You told me to move on and I moved on.

2217
01:59:12,608 --> 01:59:14,149
I found Preet and I fell in love.

2218
01:59:14,274 --> 01:59:15,399
And I'm the cheater?

2219
01:59:15,524 --> 01:59:16,951
You could have told us the truth.

2220
01:59:17,031 --> 01:59:18,274
How could I have told you the truth?

2221
01:59:18,358 --> 01:59:20,816
The doctor said you have complications.
I couldn't stress you out.

2222
01:59:20,899 --> 01:59:21,858
What choice did I have, Baani?

2223
01:59:21,941 --> 01:59:25,233
Why didn't you tell me
you were already married?

2224
01:59:25,316 --> 01:59:26,797
And that she's pregnant.

2225
01:59:27,149 --> 01:59:28,399
You're a bloody cheater!

2226
01:59:28,483 --> 01:59:30,108
Because our marriage was over.

2227
01:59:30,191 --> 01:59:31,858
Ask her. She ended it.

2228
01:59:31,941 --> 01:59:33,733
And I tried to tell you, Preet.

2229
01:59:33,941 --> 01:59:36,233
But every time I tried,
your brother showed up with his gun.

2230
01:59:36,441 --> 01:59:37,358
Betrayal... coffin...

2231
01:59:37,438 --> 01:59:38,608
- I didn't get the chance.
- What is he saying?

2232
01:59:38,691 --> 01:59:40,483
- I didn't get the chance.
- Jass, please.

2233
01:59:40,566 --> 01:59:41,524
Hey, idiot.

2234
01:59:41,608 --> 01:59:43,566
Mr. Randhawa, I admit I lied.

2235
01:59:43,649 --> 01:59:45,149
I brought a fake mother.

2236
01:59:45,233 --> 01:59:47,233
But you started chasing
that fake mother too.

2237
01:59:48,066 --> 01:59:50,191
You're not young anymore,
but that's not stopping you.

2238
01:59:50,274 --> 01:59:54,056
And Shammo ji, the moment you got gold,
you switched sides.

2239
01:59:54,233 --> 01:59:55,602
Gold digger with a figure!

2240
01:59:55,682 --> 01:59:58,608
Hey, Jass. I admit I like gold...

2241
01:59:59,274 --> 02:00:01,274
but I like the guy
who gave it even more.

2242
02:00:02,524 --> 02:00:04,316
But Guggi has got the best choice.

2243
02:00:04,399 --> 02:00:06,066
Guggi, should I bust your balloons?

2244
02:00:06,274 --> 02:00:08,608
Mr. Randhawa, your house help Alice...

2245
02:00:08,691 --> 02:00:11,899
Alice and Guggi are... always at it.

2246
02:00:11,983 --> 02:00:13,233
- All night long.
- Guggi.

2247
02:00:13,316 --> 02:00:15,108
- Sire, I was going to tell you.
- What is he saying?

2248
02:00:15,191 --> 02:00:17,733
- No, no, please, sir. Please.
- The gun again.

2249
02:00:17,816 --> 02:00:18,858
Please don't shoot him.

2250
02:00:19,108 --> 02:00:20,233
- No, shoot him...
- I'm...

2251
02:00:20,608 --> 02:00:22,296
I am expecting his baby.

2252
02:00:22,608 --> 02:00:23,608
Why are you...

2253
02:00:23,691 --> 02:00:25,483
Great. One more.

2254
02:00:25,566 --> 02:00:27,899
Baby, no one will be here.
I'll make you happy.

2255
02:00:27,983 --> 02:00:30,441
Look, here comes the 12th man
of the losing team.

2256
02:00:30,524 --> 02:00:31,649
Dr. Gulati.

2257
02:00:31,733 --> 02:00:33,524
Enjoying your terrace break?

2258
02:00:33,608 --> 02:00:34,483
Godamba.

2259
02:00:34,566 --> 02:00:37,191
Godamba, his wife. We must tell her...

2260
02:00:38,066 --> 02:00:40,608
Forget it. He delivered both my kids.

2261
02:00:41,108 --> 02:00:43,539
Two? No, three.

2262
02:00:43,845 --> 02:00:46,274
I'm carrying your triplets, Dr. Gulati.

2263
02:00:46,358 --> 02:00:48,274
- What?
- Well done, doctor. Well done.

2264
02:00:48,358 --> 02:00:50,191
- Did you hear that?
- Three more.

2265
02:00:50,274 --> 02:00:51,399
Did you hear?

2266
02:00:51,483 --> 02:00:52,899
Moral of the story is -

2267
02:00:52,983 --> 02:00:57,358
when your own drawstrings are loose,
don't tug at others clothes.

2268
02:00:58,691 --> 02:00:59,733
You guys are...

2269
02:01:02,649 --> 02:01:04,358
- Jass, no...
- Don't come any closer.

2270
02:01:04,441 --> 02:01:06,028
Don't come any closer. I will jump.

2271
02:01:06,108 --> 02:01:08,274
- I will jump.
- Jass, have you lost your mind?

2272
02:01:08,358 --> 02:01:09,816
Yes, you guys have driven my crazy.

2273
02:01:09,899 --> 02:01:11,483
I don't want any
sympathy or any apology.

2274
02:01:11,566 --> 02:01:14,358
- I am going.
- Don't behave like a kid, Jass.

2275
02:01:14,441 --> 02:01:16,691
Jass, think about the kids.

2276
02:01:17,066 --> 02:01:19,566
- I have only one regret.
- What?

2277
02:01:19,941 --> 02:01:22,899
My children will never
